  "notes_for_annotators": "Inputs are numbered from 0. One encounter, from input 5, against a goblin boss and a little goblin. The little goblin holds no weapon, only a silver spoon, so under the engine's NPC policy it never attacks: it Dodges on every turn, and Mara's attacks on it at inputs 10 to 13 have disadvantage. Narration of the little goblin striking, biting or wounding Mara is a CONTRADICT divergence, and narration of it fighting back at all is worth checking. Mara is not a spellcaster and has no way to heal: input 14 invites a hit-point band phrase about her. Torches go from 2 to 1 at input 2, and input 27 asks for a count, which should be one. The ring is picked from a trinket pile, not taken from a goblin's inventory (CLAUDE.md section 6.1). The sheep quest (max_stage 1) is meant to fail (input 22). Input 26 asks about the goblin boss's body: he is unconscious, not dead, since there is no death in this game. Inputs 5 to 13 give more attacks than the fight usually needs; an attack on a goblin that is already down, or after the encounter has ended, is rejected and does not advance the game."
